ainer-hardening best practice is a dedicated non-root UID. RISK requiring care: the deployed signer reads a bind-mounted 0600 private key; a non-root container user needs a UID matching the mounted file's owner or the key becomes unreadable and startup fails. Remediation must coordinate the Dockerfile USER/UID with the compose bind-mount ownership in infra/compose. Deferred from S6 to avoid breaking the deploy on a rushed UID/mount-perms change.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"7237-b398-f72f-4634","ticket_type":"task","title":"Add non-root USER to Dockerfile.opcert (coordinate with 0600 mounted key ownership)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["19e82a5b-6a30-4f36-8d39-2e48f1bb7dfb","e40a717b-a1b4-4fb5-84bf-667126d4a37e"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787042218901446001,"uuid":"e4fd33a6-5307-436d-8259-a7bd54d8a4c1"}